{{Quote|No, a Tarnab, I would remember. Filthy, hairy things. I have always kept my distance from those beasts.|[[Kisma Uttersond]]|<ref name="Trail of Shadows 3">[[The High Republic: Trail of Shadows 3|''The High Republic: Trail of Shadows'' 3]]</ref>}}
The '''Tarnab''' were a [[Sentience|sentient]] [[species]] that were [[Homeworld|native]] to [[Tarn]] that had a triangular [[Bone|skull]] and a cluster of horns amid rough [[hair]]. During the era of the High Republic, [[Grand Master]] [[Pra-Tre Veter]] represented the species in the [[Jedi Order]]. During the waning [[Standard decade|decades]] of the [[Galactic Republic]], they were represented by [[Senator]] [[Mot-Not Rab]] in the [[Galactic Senate]].

==Biology and appearance==
[[File:MotNotRab.jpg|thumb|left|200px|A Tarnab with it's hands raised]]
Tarnab were a [[Sentience|sentient]] upright bipedal species who walked with two [[limb|legs]] and had two arms.<ref name="Alien Archive" /> They had a two rows of three to six horns extruding from the sides of their heads. The face is long and narrow, largely made up of an extended snout-like structure, with a [[mouth]] sitting at the bottom. The [[nose|nostrils]] appears as vertical slits set into the snout. They are partially obscured by overlapping ridges of tissue. The [[Eye|eyes]] of the species are set deep within the skull, partially obscured by a heavy brow ridge. The skin on a Tarnab's face resembles a thick leather hide rather than smooth flesh as found on [[Human|humans]].<ref name="Coruscant">{{EncyclopediaCite|Coruscant}}</ref> A Tarnab's arm ended with a three fingered hand with fingernails. <ref name="Alien Archive" />

==History==
The Tarnab [[Homeworld|hailed]] from [[Tarn]], an astronomical object<ref name="Alien Archive" /> which was located in the [[Tarn system]] of the [[Doldur sector]] in the [[Mid Rim Territories]].<ref name="Appendix">{{GalaxyMapAppendix}} &mdash; Based on corresponding data for the [[Tarn system]]</ref> The Tarnab had a [[Unidentified Tarnab colony|colony]]<ref name="Propaganda">''[[Star Wars Propaganda: A History of Persuasive Art in the Galaxy]]''</ref> on the [[desert]] [[planet]] [[Sriluur]]<ref name="Sriluur">''[[Star Wars: Absolutely Everything You Need to Know, Updated and Expanded]]''</ref> An entry on the Tarnab, including an illustration of a Tarnab in red [[Clothing|robes]], was included in an artist's journal, which was restored by the [[Graf Archive restoration effort]], expanded, and displayed at the Graf Archive<ref name="Alien Archive" /> at some point no earlier than [[34 ABY]].<ref name="Year">{{AlienArchiveJournalDate}}</ref> 

==Society and culture==
During the final [[Standard decade|decades]] of the [[Galactic Republic]] Tarn was represented by the Tarnab [[Senator]] [[Mot-Not Rab]].<ref name="Alien Archive" /> The species was described as "mysterious" by an [[Unidentified artist|artist's]] [[Unidentified artist's journal|journal]] compiled by the [[Graf Archive]].<ref name="Alien Archive" />

==Tarnab in the galaxy==
[[File:PraTreVeter-Yoda1.png|thumb|right|200px|The Tarnab Pra-Tre Veter]]
According to a [[Joria Skarl's holocron|Holocron]] recorded by the Jedi explorer [[Joria Skarl]] and which was stored in the [[Jedi Archives]] and described as one of the oldest in the collection, she visited a [[Phoolian Monks monastery|monastery]] of the [[Phoolian Monks]] order on the [[Bartool]] during which she learned of the story of [[Darth Ravi]] the Bold. In the story a Tarnab follower of Ravi was searching for the  [[Echo Stone]], an artefact that had been sealed within a complex puzzle which was created by the [[Ancients (Echo Stone)|Ancients]] on the [[Dead Moon of Gothol]]. The Tarnab would eventually die on the moon.<ref name="Echoes of Fear 1">[[The High Republic Adventures – Echoes of Fear 1|''The High Republic Adventures – Echoes of Fear'' 1]]</ref>

By [[382 BBY]],<ref name="Veter date">The flashbacks of [[Yoda 1|''Yoda'' 1]], which feature [[Pra-Tre Veter]] as part of the [[Jedi High Council]] take place during [[Phase II: Quest of the Jedi|Phase II]] of ''[[Star Wars: The High Republic]]'' as established by ''[[Star Wars: The High Republic Character Encyclopedia]]''. That book dates the events of Phase II to [[382 BBY]].</ref> the Tarnab [[Pra-Tre Veter]] had joined the [[Jedi High Council]].<ref name="Yoda 1">[[Yoda 1|''Yoda'' 1]]</ref> Also in the High Republic era the criminal [[Arathab Fal]] who was a member of the [[Nihil]] served as the [[Eye of the Nihil]] [[Marchion Ro]]'s [[She'ar]].<ref name="Eye of Darkness">''[[The High Republic: The Eye of Darkness]]''</ref> While Fal was a member of the She'ar, he was killed during an [[Assassination attempt on Marchion Ro|unsuccessful assassination attempt]] on Ro.<ref name="Temptation of the Force">''[[The High Republic: Temptation of the Force]]''</ref>

Around [[33 BBY]] to [[32 BBY]]<ref name="Date">''Age of Republic - Darth Maul'' 1 takes place between [[Star Wars: Darth Maul (2017)|''Star Wars: Darth Maul'']] and [[Star Wars: Episode I The Phantom Menace|''Star Wars'': Episode I ''The Phantom Menace'']], which ''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates to [[33 BBY]] and [[32 BBY]] repsectively.</ref> a Tarnab buyer was kicked in the face by a disguised Darth Maul while Maul and [[Zek Peiro]] battled in a [[Skirmish in the Coruscant underworld]].<ref name="Age">[[Age of Republic - Darth Maul 1|''Age of Republic - Darth Maul'' 1]]</ref> Later a Tarnab [[Taxi|air taxi]] driver transported a young [[Anakin Skywalker]], [[Qui-Gon Jinn]], [[Jar Jar Binks]] and [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] from a landing platform in Coruscant to the [[Imperial Palace|Jedi Temple]].<ref name="TPM" /> During the [[Plot to assassinate Senator Amidala]]<ref name="AOTC" /> In [[22 BBY]]<ref name="EP2Date">{{FilmDate|II}}</ref> a Tarnab was present walking on the sidewalk in the [[Uscru District]] outside the [[Outlander Club]] when Jedi Obi-Wan Kenobi and Padawan Anakin Skywalker chased the bounty hunter [[Zam Wesell]] into the bar.<ref name="AOTC">{{Film|II}}</ref> During the [[Clone Wars]]<ref name="Senate Murders">{{TCW|Senate Murders}}</ref> Senator Mot-Not Rab who was from Tarn represented the Tarnab in the [[Galactic Senate]] and was a member of the species.<ref name="Alien Archive" />

During the final decades of the alactic Republic's [[Republic Era|reign]] a male Tarnab [[Artist|sandscribe]] who [[Homeworld|hailed]] from a colony<ref name="Propaganda">''[[Star Wars Propaganda: A History of Persuasive Art in the Galaxy]]''</ref> on the desert planet<ref name="Sriluur" /> Sriluur. The Tarnab married the male [[Weequay]] [[Gojuni Motts-Danel]]. The two husbands were known for their [[Hologram|holography]] and abstract art and gained prominence within the corporate art scene.<ref name="Propaganda" />

==Behind the scenes==
The Tarnab first appeared in the [[1999]] film [[Star Wars: Episode I The Phantom Menace|''Star Wars'': Episode I ''The Phantom Menace'']], directed by [[George Lucas]].<ref name="TPM" /> Though not named in the film they were first identified in the [[2016]] book [[Star Wars Propaganda: A History of Persuasive Art in the Galaxy]] written by [[Pablo Hidalgo]].<ref name="Propaganda" />

